course: dictionary
lesson: 10557
title: Unbuckle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A buckle is the clip that holds a belt, strap or seat belt closed. To unbuckle is to undo that clip so the strap comes loose. The start of the word, un-, often means "undo", as in untie or unlock, so you can work out the meaning from the part you already know.
explain: «An unbuckled helmet comes off in a crash before the head hits the ground.» The clue is comes off: if the strap is undone, the helmet is free to fly off. So unbuckled must mean its fastening was undone.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it: «An undone helmet comes off in a crash...» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. You can unbuckle a belt, a shoe, a bike helmet strap or a backpack.
fact: To unbuckle means to undo a buckle, opening the fastening of a belt, strap or seat belt.
fact: The prefix un- often means "undo", as in untie, unlock and unbuckle.
fact: Phrases you may hear are: unbuckle your seat belt, unbuckle a belt, unbuckle the strap.
fact: «Unbuckled» is the past tense, so it means the buckle was already undone.
fact: In a car, keep your seat belt buckled until the car has stopped and a grown-up says it is safe to unbuckle.
exercise: «An unbuckled helmet comes off in a crash before the head hits the ground.» What does unbuckled mean here? | Put on very tightly | *Had its strap undone | Too small for the head | Painted bright red
exercise: In a car, when should you unbuckle your seat belt? | As soon as the car starts moving | Whenever you feel a bit hot | *When the car has stopped and a grown-up says it is safe | While the car is going fast on the motorway
exercise: The word unbuckle is made of un- and buckle. What does un- often mean? | *Undo | Loud | Happy | Very big
test: «On a flight the plane hit sudden bumpy air, and a boy who had unbuckled was thrown up against the ceiling.» Why was the boy hurt? | He was belted in tightly | He was sitting on the wing | *He had undone his seat belt | He had fallen asleep
test: Which of these things can you unbuckle? | The moon | The weather | The sun | *Your bike helmet strap
exam: Ava reads «Unbuckle your seat belt once the car has stopped.» What does unbuckle mean? | To pull the car door shut | *To undo the fastening | To lock the windows | To tighten the strap
